From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:19:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: meson-sm1-odroid-hc4: fix up the SPI NOR pins and
 speed

Two defects in the flash node, both of which U-Boot inherits from the
upstream device tree it builds against.

The flash is wired with six lines, but nor_pins describes only four of
them - data, clock and chip select.  HOLD# (BOOT_3) and WP# (BOOT_7) are
claimed by nobody, so they keep whatever the boot ROM left them as.
Booting from the SPI it muxes them to the nor function and the flash
works; booting from SD past the SPI - the button underneath the board -
it leaves them as eMMC data lines pulled low, and the flash stays silent.
Claim them in a board-local group rather than adding them to nor_pins:
that group is shared with boards that keep the eMMC enabled over
BOOT_0..7, while the HC4 disables it.

The node also asks for 104 MHz, at which reads come back corrupted - the
first byte of a transfer has bit 0 flipped from 0 to 1 part of the time.
That breaks writing the bootloader, since flashcp verifies as it goes and
aborts partway through.  Hardkernel's own device tree runs the flash at
40 MHz, where the same tests come back clean.

Tested on ODROID-HC4 with an XT25F128B.

Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 dts/upstream/src/arm64/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts | 14 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts
--- a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts
+++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/amlogic/meson-sm1-odroid-hc4.dts
@@ -122,21 +122,31 @@
 
 &sd_emmc_c {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+&periphs_pinctrl {
+	hc4_nor_hold_wp_pins: nor-hold-wp {
+		mux {
+			groups = "nor_hold", "nor_wp";
+			function = "nor";
+			bias-disable;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &spifc {
 	status = "okay";
-	pinctrl-0 = <&nor_pins>;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&nor_pins>, <&hc4_nor_hold_wp_pins>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 
 	flash@0 {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
 		compatible = "jedec,spi-nor";
 		reg = <0>;
-		spi-max-frequency = <104000000>;
+		spi-max-frequency = <40000000>;
 	};
 };
 
 &usb {
 	phys = <&usb2_phy0>, <&usb2_phy1>;
